{
  "requirement": "An application-supplied assessment procedure can perform ordinary computation\nand request zero or more typed model answers. It can use intermediate answers\nin later computation and requests, then return its `Criterion::Ok` value.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.procedures` asks for four things. A procedure can do ordinary computation. It can request zero or more typed model answers. It can use intermediate answers in later computation and requests. It returns its `Criterion::Ok` value. The three marked tests cover these as follows.\n\n- **Zero requests, plus ordinary computation and the returned value:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` runs `Review` through `Memory::run_review` with `ask_in_callback` false and no agent. The procedure makes no model request and still completes. The test asserts that the returned `Assessment` has `result == false` for node 9. It also asserts that `started == [9]` and that a later `verify` returns the replacement value.\n- **Multiple requests and intermediate answers:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` sets `ask_in_callback`. `run_review` then makes a first typed `ask::<Answer>()` with the current node contents. It makes a second request whose context is `format!(\"Check intermediate result {}\", first.n)`, built from the first answer. The test asserts exactly 2 requests. It asserts that the second request's text is \"Check intermediate result 7\", so the first answer fed the later request. It also asserts that the returned value has `result == true`, and that the evidence is stored with the expected dependency.\n- **Typed answers and several independent requests:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls]` issues two `ask::<Answer>()` calls. It asserts the decoded typed fields (`n == 7` and `n == 11`). It also checks that two requests reached the agent.\n\nThe zero-request case, the multi-request case with intermediate use, the typed answer and the returned `Ok` value are each asserted. The text names no boundary or failure case beyond these. Error handling for a missing agent or an invalid submission belongs to other requirements, which have their own tests, for example `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error`. The tests carry {test} markers for the subject. No gaps and no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "37048cdb28d1833f5f6039462c706ae2a75137cb6c0136cd21529300ad153191",
